Description: Modern PDF editor with an embedded terminal
 TermiPDF is a PyQt6 desktop PDF editor with a built-in terminal for
 batch operations.
 .
 Features:
  * View PDFs (single-page or continuous-scroll), zoom, fit-to-window,
    outline (TOC) sidebar, thumbnail rail.
  * Annotate with freehand ink, multi-colour highlights, sticky notes,
    shapes (rect, ellipse, arrow), and Unicode text insertion
    (including Bangla).
  * Edit pages: delete, rotate, swap, split, merge, reorder, extract,
    and generate new PDFs from current pages.
  * Tools: QR-share popups, page-level image-to-PDF conversion,
    full-text search with auto-highlight, undo/redo, save.
  * Themes: dark (Dracula/Nord) and light (Edge-like), auto-detected
    from your OS preference, persisted across sessions.
  * Embedded terminal docks at the bottom of the window and exposes
    every feature as a typed command - type `help` to list them all.
